 "notes": [
  "calls 1 and 3 are the two populations' FIRST evaluation (A cold, B rebuilt-but-equal); calls 2 and 4 are the identity fast path doing its job on each, and an identity hit leaves the content table untouched (attempts 0 -- not a content miss)",
  "a content hit is served only after ONE decode, which is what the content key needs to prove the programs; the merge, the trace and the compile are what it skips",
  "null, never false: an expectation the route exposes no counter for stays None (a pre-round tree has no content table and no stage timers)",
  "evogp.tree.batch_engine.batch_content_stats() is unavailable on this tree: every content counter is null (NOT zero) and the reuse verdict stays None for the content-keyed expectations. The measured before/after evidence is then the PLAN table: the rebuilt population pays a plan MISS (re-decode, re-trace, re-merge) instead of being served",
  "evogp.tree.batch_engine.batch_stage_stats() is unavailable on this tree: every stage counter is null (NOT zero), so 'it skipped trace/merge/compile' cannot be read off stage call counts here -- the merge work is visible only through the plan/exec counters and call_ms"
 ]
